1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,663
A verified program still has to talk to a
world nobody verified.

2
00:00:04,663 --> 00:00:07,941
The question is what it is allowed to
assume.

3
00:00:08,867 --> 00:00:10,781
Effects do not disappear.

4
00:00:10,781 --> 00:00:12,389
They become explicit.

5
00:00:12,389 --> 00:00:17,443
IO is a type, and a function that prints
says so in its signature.

6
00:00:17,443 --> 00:00:31,149
Pure-looking code can still run at
imperative speed: an array is a value in
the type system and a mutable buffer in
the implementation, updated in place when
it is uniquely owned.

7
00:00:32,367 --> 00:00:37,483
Real programs need the world: files,
sockets, databases, time.

8
00:00:37,483 --> 00:00:42,352
Lean can call almost anything, so a
binding is a few lines.

9
00:00:42,352 --> 00:00:46,808
But a binding is not a library you can
verify against.

10
00:00:46,808 --> 00:00:49,036
A binding says how to call.

11
00:00:49,036 --> 00:00:55,720
A theory says what the call means, and
contracts are written against the meaning.

12
00:00:56,933 --> 00:00:59,279
Every theory ends in an assertion.

13
00:00:59,279 --> 00:01:04,247
The operating system, the network card,
the database, are not vericoded.

14
00:01:04,247 --> 00:01:07,974
So the bottom of the stack is exactly what
you assume.

15
00:01:07,974 --> 00:01:17,910
Keep the assumption small, explicit, and
testable: differential testing against the
real system, property-based checks,
fuzzing at the boundary.

16
00:01:19,233 --> 00:01:20,802
What to build first?

17
00:01:20,802 --> 00:01:23,548
Rank by dependents, then by purity.

18
00:01:23,548 --> 00:01:31,000
Files first, because everything sits on
them, and specify the failures, not only
the successes.

19
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,747
Then text: Unicode and regular expressions
are pure, so they can be proved end to
end.

20
00:01:37,747 --> 00:01:42,532
Then time, with the wall clock may jump as
an explicit axiom.

21
00:01:42,532 --> 00:01:44,964
Then JSON and the wire formats.

22
00:01:46,167 --> 00:01:53,307
Vericoding moves the work to the surface
where a machine can check it: what the
program must mean.

23
00:01:53,307 --> 00:01:55,055
Write the specification.

24
00:01:55,055 --> 00:01:56,877
Let the proof be checked.

